<title>FRANCE: French 1997 deficit as percentage of GDP - table.</title>
<headline>French 1997 deficit as percentage of GDP - table.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government gave the following breakdown showing how it plans to reduce the total public deficit to three percent of gross domestic product in 1997:</p>
<p>					    1995    1996     1997</p>
<p>Central government deficit</p>
<p> - Deficit pre-income tax reform  -4.2    -3.65    -3.15</p>
<p> - Income tax reform		   n/a     n/a     -0.30</p>
<p> - Adjustment to EU standards     +0.2    +0.15    +0.10</p>
<p> - France Telecom payment	    n/a     n/a     +0.45</p>
<p> - Total				  -4.0    -3.5     -2.90</p>
<p>Social security deficit</p>
<p> - general				-0.95   -0.65    -0.35</p>
<p> - other (including unemployment) +0.10   +0.05    +0.05</p>
<p> - Total				  -0.85   -0.60    -0.30</p>
<p>Other public spending</p>
<p> - Central public bodies	    +0.20   +0.15    +0.20</p>
<p> - Local authorities		  -0.20   -0.05     0.00</p>
<p> - Total				   0.00   +0.10    +0.20</p>
<p> TOTAL PUBLIC DEFICIT		 -4.85   -4.00    -3.00</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
